Subject: [PATCH 4/4] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc7: the publication tests'
 synthetic runs hold a plan that reconciles

The whole suite on 0073277 failed 7 tests in test_publish.py and test_recovery_and_rollback.py: they publish
synthetic runs created directly in the database, with exports but no plan, and 1.10.0rc7's publication reads
the coverage again and refuses a run whose plan has no listing ("the run's plan has no listing"). That
refusal is intended (such a run carries no evidence of what it covered), so the tests change, not the code:
tests/integration/helpers.py gains reconciled_plan (one listing read to its last page: a store-bound page
listing every record's UPC, each observed on that page, placed under the listing and recorded fresh), and
test_publish.py's prepared_run uses it. A new test checks that a run without a plan, or whose page lists one
product with no record, is refused with the pointer and latest.json untouched. No source file changes.
